Arbat Street: Heart of Moscow’s Culture.
Location: In the very centre of Moscow, just west of the Kremlin.
What you can find there: Arbat is a historic pedestrian street lined with colourful 19th‑century buildings. Here you’ll find:
• souvenir shops and art galleries;
• cosy cafés and traditional Russian restaurants;
• street artists and musicians;
• handicraft stalls and bookshops.
What you can do there:
• take a leisurely walk and admire the architecture;
• listen to live street performances;
• buy unique souvenirs;
• enjoy a meal with a view of city life;
• capture memorable photos of this iconic spot.
A must‑visit for every tourist in Moscow!
